<title>MEXICO: Mexico 96-97 coffee crop output by state - council.</title>
<headline>Mexico 96-97 coffee crop output by state - council.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican Coffee Council released Wednesday a state-by-state breakdown of coffee output from the 1996-1997 cycle. (Figures in 60-kg bags)</p>
<p>    Cycle	  94-95		95-96		96-97</p>
<p>    Chiapas    1,304,390	 1,476,420	 1,742,600</p>
<p>    Veracruz   1,053,310	 1,601,310	 1,173,730</p>
<p>    Oaxaca	 663,530	   778,750	   736,410</p>
<p>    Puebla	 617,310	   922,770	   809,930</p>
<p>    Guerrero     167,130	   228,090	   231,020</p>
<p>    Hidalgo	149,630	   174,200	   190,210</p>
<p>    San Luis	75,200	    82,520	    74,910</p>
<p>    Nayarit	 99,230	   102,220	   109,530</p>
<p>    Jalisco	  6,640	     8,620	     9,380</p>
<p>    Tabasco	  7,180	     7,410	     7,220</p>
<p>    Colima	  14,380	    15,810	    13,590</p>
<p>    Queretaro	1,740	     1,820	     1,370</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530)) E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
</text>
